# Deployment topology

This repository uses `{{ topology }}` topology and `{{ architecture }}` internal architecture. Those are separate decisions: topology defines deployable boundaries; architecture defines dependencies inside each boundary.

{% if topology == 'single-deployable' -%}
There is one deployable unit. Keep internal boundaries explicit so deployment simplicity does not become unstructured coupling.
{% elif topology == 'modular-monolith' -%}
Capability modules share one deployment but own their contracts and data access. The module dependency graph is acyclic; cross-module access goes through public interfaces.
{% else -%}
Services deploy independently. Each service owns its data, compatibility policy, operational health, and release lifecycle. Network calls require timeouts, retry budgets, idempotency where applicable, and observable failure handling.
{% endif %}
